{
  "//": [
    "Cases for the differential check in tools/trace-conformance.sh: every one",
    "is run through BOTH packages/trace-format/validate.ts and the specification's",
    "own ajv + trace-v1.schema.json, and the two must agree on accept/reject.",
    "",
    "The specification's fixtures cannot do this job. They are all CONFORMANT, so",
    "they only ever exercise the accept direction -- a transcription that is too",
    "lax passes all 16 and is wrong. That is not hypothetical: this table was",
    "added after `2024-01-15T10:00:60Z` was found accepted here and rejected by",
    "ajv, with the corpus green.",
    "",
    "ONE REJECTION PER CHECK validate.ts MAKES, which is a stronger claim than",
    "one per schema rule and the one worth holding: a rule enforced by two call",
    "sites needs two cases, or deleting either leaves this green. Each was",
    "verified by deleting its check and watching the verdicts diverge -- that is",
    "the only thing that tells a covering case from a decorative one.",
    "",
    "The date-time rows are the largest block because `format: date-time` is not",
    "RFC 3339 here: it is whatever ajv-formats implements, which admits a",
    "whitespace separator and the `+0100` and `+01` offset spellings the grammar",
    "does not. See SPEC-FEEDBACK.md finding 6."
  ],
